course: dictionary
lesson: 5813
title: Magnets: what they pull and what they don't
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A magnet is a piece of iron or other material that pulls certain things towards it. Scientists say it attracts them. Magnets attract iron, steel, nickel and cobalt, but not wood, plastic, paper, copper or aluminium. «Big magnets pull out steel cans, while aluminium, which is not magnetic, is separated in other ways.»
explain: Every magnet has two ends, called poles: a north pole and a south pole. Opposite poles attract, so they pull together. Like poles repel, so they push apart. «A compass needle is a small magnet free to turn, and it lines up with the Earth's magnetic field.» That is why a compass points north: the Earth is like a huge magnet.
explain: The word magnet can also mean a person or place that attracts many people. «The park is a magnet for families» means that lots of families want to go there, as if the park pulls them in, just like a magnet pulls iron.
explain: Magnets are useful, but some can be dangerous. «Strong magnets are kept away from bank cards and electronics,» because they can damage them. Small magnets must never be swallowed: two can pinch the gut and cause serious harm.
fact: A magnet is a piece of iron or other material that attracts iron and steel.
fact: Magnets attract iron, steel, nickel and cobalt, but not wood, plastic, paper, copper or aluminium.
fact: Every magnet has a north pole and a south pole.
fact: Opposite poles attract, and like poles repel (push apart).
fact: The Earth is like a huge magnet, which is why a compass points north.
exercise: «Big magnets pull out steel cans, while aluminium, which is not magnetic, is separated in other ways.» Which of these would a magnet pull towards it? | *A steel nail | Plastic | Paper | Wood
exercise: Which metal is a magnet attracted to? | Aluminium | *Iron | Wood | Copper
exercise: «A compass needle is a small magnet free to turn, and it lines up with the Earth's magnetic field.» Why does a compass point north? | *Because the Earth is like a huge magnet | Because the needle is made of wood | Because north is always the warmest place | Because the needle is made of plastic
test: When the same poles of two magnets are brought together, what happens? | They pull together | They melt | *They push apart | They stick and never separate
test: «The park is a magnet for families.» What does magnet mean here? | A small switch that turns on a light | *A place that attracts many people | A kind of wooden toy | A piece of iron that pulls metal
exam: Why must small magnets never be swallowed? | They taste sweet and make you ill | *They can pinch the gut and are very dangerous | They make your teeth stronger | They turn your skin into metal
